        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="1088" n="994" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg994"/>

                <head>No. 618.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 16,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 185.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch from our consul-general at Havana in further relation to extreme
                    annoyances of the passport arrangements in Cuba.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>




